cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use MEMBRANE in your research, please cite it using the
  metadata below. No official GitHub release/tag has been published
  yet -- `version` below is a pre-release research-candidate label,
  and `commit` names the exact commit this metadata reflects, not a
  tagged release. See docs/v0.1.0-research-release-plan.md for the
  proposed first tagged release and docs/research-release-freeze.md
  for this repository's current release status.
title: >-
  MEMBRANE: A Research Prototype for Mixed-Precision, Exact-Retrieval
  LLM KV-Cache Memory
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Altıntaş
    given-names: Kadir Eren
repository-code: "https://github.com/kadireren7/membrane"
version: "0.1.0-research-candidate"
commit: 58ec90b
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  MEMBRANE is a research codebase exploring mixed-precision KV-cache
  tiering, exact (non-approximate) sparse KV retrieval, near-memory/CXL
  appliance simulation, bit-exact CPU quantization verified against
  ggml's own reference implementation, and a synthesizable FPGA
  quant/dequant datapath cosimulated in Verilator. All results are
  measured against real captured attention/KV traces from actual
  llama.cpp inference on two open SmolLM2 checkpoints, or explicitly
  labeled as simulated/assumed where no physical hardware exists. See
  the repository's README.md and docs/results-summary.md for the full,
  sourced set of findings, including negative results.
